# The build context is the repo root (`docker build -f apps/<app>/Dockerfile .`), and the Dockerfiles run
# `COPY . .`. Whatever is not needed to install and build must stay out: it would end up in a layer of the builder
# stage, and secrets would end up in the image's build cache.

# dependencies and build output are rebuilt inside the image
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/coverage
**/junit
**/*.log

# env files: the real ones are git-ignored and hold secrets, the *.example templates are not needed to build
**/.env
**/.env.*

# VCS and CI
.git
.github

# git-ignored scratch: plan workspaces, review diffs, task briefs
.superpowers

# editors and OS
.idea
.vscode
.DS_Store

# documentation, deployment files and tests are not part of the images
docs
*.md
load
deploy
docker-compose*.yaml
**/test
